@@git|common|Distributed version control for tracking source code.
- See the current branch and changed files:

`git status`

- Show a compact commit graph for every branch:

`git log --oneline --graph --decorate --all`

- Create and switch to a new branch:

`git switch -c {{feature-name}}`
@@git-commit|common|Record staged changes in the Git history.
- Stage chosen files and commit them:

`git add {{file1 file2}} && git commit -m "{{message}}"`

- Amend the most recent commit without changing its message:

`git commit --amend --no-edit`
@@git-rebase|common|Replay commits on top of another branch.
- Rebase the current branch on the latest main branch:

`git fetch origin && git rebase origin/main`

- Interactively edit the last five commits:

`git rebase -i HEAD~5`
@@gh|common|Work with GitHub from the command line.
- Create a pull request interactively:

`gh pr create`

- Show checks for the current branch's pull request:

`gh pr checks`
@@docker|common|Build and run applications in containers.
- List running containers:

`docker ps`

- Run an interactive, temporary Ubuntu container:

`docker run --rm -it ubuntu bash`

- Show recent logs and keep following them:

`docker logs -f {{container}}`
@@docker-compose|common|Run a multi-container application described by a Compose file.
- Start services in the background and build changed images:

`docker compose up -d --build`

- Stop services and remove their containers and networks:

`docker compose down`
@@kubectl|common|Control Kubernetes clusters.
- List pods in every namespace:

`kubectl get pods --all-namespaces`

- Follow logs from a deployment:

`kubectl logs -f deployment/{{name}}`

- Open a shell in a pod:

`kubectl exec -it {{pod}} -- sh`
@@helm|common|Manage Kubernetes packages with Helm.
- Install or upgrade a release from a chart:

`helm upgrade --install {{release}} {{chart}} --namespace {{namespace}} --create-namespace`

- List releases in every namespace:

`helm list --all-namespaces`
@@terraform|common|Provision infrastructure from declarative configuration.
- Format and validate the current configuration:

`terraform fmt -recursive && terraform validate`

- Preview and then apply changes:

`terraform plan -out={{plan.tfplan}} && terraform apply {{plan.tfplan}}`
@@ansible|common|Automate remote system configuration.
- Ping every host in an inventory:

`ansible all -i {{inventory.ini}} -m ping`

- Run a playbook with an inventory:

`ansible-playbook -i {{inventory.ini}} {{playbook.yml}}`
@@aws|common|Manage Amazon Web Services resources.
- Show the active caller identity:

`aws sts get-caller-identity`

- List S3 buckets:

`aws s3 ls`
@@az|common|Manage Microsoft Azure resources.
- Sign in and show the current account:

`az login && az account show`

- List resource groups as a table:

`az group list --output table`
@@gcloud|common|Manage Google Cloud resources.
- Set the active project:

`gcloud config set project {{project-id}}`

- List Compute Engine instances:

`gcloud compute instances list`
@@npm|common|Manage JavaScript packages and project scripts.
- Install project dependencies exactly from the lockfile:

`npm ci`

- Run a package script and pass it extra arguments:

`npm run {{script}} -- {{arguments}}`
@@npx|common|Run a command from an npm package.
- Run a package without installing it globally:

`npx {{package}} {{arguments}}`

- Force a particular package version:

`npx {{package}}@{{version}} {{arguments}}`
@@yarn|common|Manage JavaScript packages with Yarn.
- Install locked project dependencies:

`yarn install --immutable`

- Add a development dependency:

`yarn add --dev {{package}}`
@@pnpm|common|Manage JavaScript packages with a space-efficient store.
- Install project dependencies:

`pnpm install`

- Run a package script across workspace projects:

`pnpm --recursive run {{script}}`
@@node|common|Run JavaScript with Node.js.
- Execute a JavaScript file:

`node {{script.js}} {{arguments}}`

- Evaluate an expression:

`node --eval '{{console.log(expression)}}'`
@@python|common|Run Python programs and modules.
- Run a module using the selected interpreter:

`python -m {{module}} {{arguments}}`

- Start a local web server on port 8000:

`python -m http.server 8000`
@@pip|common|Install and manage Python packages.
- Install packages from a requirements file:

`python -m pip install -r requirements.txt`

- Show packages with newer versions available:

`python -m pip list --outdated`
@@uv|common|Manage fast Python environments, dependencies, and tools.
- Create an environment and install locked dependencies:

`uv sync`

- Run a command inside the project environment:

`uv run {{command}}`
@@cargo|common|Build and manage Rust projects.
- Check a project without producing final binaries:

`cargo check`

- Run all tests, including their output:

`cargo test -- --nocapture`
@@go|common|Build and manage Go code.
- Run all tests below the current module:

`go test ./...`

- Format and simplify all packages:

`gofmt -w .`
@@dotnet|common|Build and run .NET applications.
- Create a console application:

`dotnet new console -n {{ProjectName}}`

- Restore, build, and run tests:

`dotnet restore && dotnet build && dotnet test`
@@curl|common|Transfer data to or from a URL.
- Follow redirects and save using the remote filename:

`curl -LO {{https://example.com/file}}`

- Send JSON in a POST request:

`curl -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{{"key":"value"}}' {{url}}`
@@wget|common|Download files from the web.
- Download a file to a chosen path:

`wget -O {{output.file}} {{url}}`

- Continue a partially completed download:

`wget -c {{url}}`
@@ssh|common|Open a secure shell on a remote machine.
- Connect using a username and port:

`ssh -p {{port}} {{user}}@{{host}}`

- Forward a local port to a service reachable by the server:

`ssh -L {{local-port}}:{{destination-host}}:{{destination-port}} {{user}}@{{server}}`
@@scp|common|Copy files over SSH.
- Copy a local file to a remote directory:

`scp {{file}} {{user}}@{{host}}:{{/remote/path/}}`

- Recursively copy a remote directory locally:

`scp -r {{user}}@{{host}}:{{/remote/directory}} {{local-directory}}`
@@rsync|common|Synchronize files locally or over SSH.
- Copy a directory while preserving metadata and showing progress:

`rsync -avh --progress {{source/}} {{destination/}}`

- Preview a remote synchronization that deletes extra destination files:

`rsync -avhn --delete {{source/}} {{user}}@{{host}}:{{destination/}}`
@@grep|common|Find lines matching a text pattern.
- Search recursively with line numbers and ignore case:

`grep -Rni -- '{{pattern}}' {{directory}}`

- Show lines that do not match:

`grep -v -- '{{pattern}}' {{file}}`
@@rg|common|Recursively search text with ripgrep.
- Search hidden files while respecting ignore files:

`rg --hidden '{{pattern}}' {{path}}`

- List files whose contents match a pattern:

`rg -l '{{pattern}}'`
@@find|common|Find files and directories by their properties.
- Find files by case-insensitive extension:

`find {{directory}} -type f -iname '*.{{ext}}'`

- Find files changed within the last day:

`find {{directory}} -type f -mtime -1`
@@sed|common|Transform text using editing expressions.
- Replace every occurrence in a stream:

`sed 's/{{old}}/{{new}}/g' {{file}}`

- Print a selected range of lines:

`sed -n '{{10,20}}p' {{file}}`
@@awk|common|Process structured lines of text.
- Print the first and third whitespace-separated fields:

`awk '{print $1, $3}' {{file}}`

- Sum the values in the second field:

`awk '{sum += $2} END {print sum}' {{file}}`
@@jq|common|Query and transform JSON.
- Pretty-print JSON from a file:

`jq . {{file.json}}`

- Select objects and print one property:

`jq '.[] | select(.enabled == true) | .name' {{file.json}}`
@@tar|common|Create and extract tar archives.
- Create a compressed archive from a directory:

`tar -czf {{archive.tar.gz}} {{directory}}`

- Extract a compressed archive into a directory:

`tar -xzf {{archive.tar.gz}} -C {{directory}}`
@@chmod|common|Change file permission bits.
- Make a script executable by its owner:

`chmod u+x {{script}}`

- Recursively give directories 755 and files 644 permissions:

`find {{path}} -type d -exec chmod 755 {} + && find {{path}} -type f -exec chmod 644 {} +`
@@ps|common|Show information about running processes.
- Show every process with full details:

`ps aux`

- Find processes by a case-insensitive name:

`ps aux | grep -i '[{{p}}]rocess-name'`
@@kill|common|Send a signal to a process.
- Ask a process to terminate normally:

`kill {{pid}}`

- Force termination only when a normal request did not work:

`kill -KILL {{pid}}`
@@lsof|common|List files and network sockets opened by processes.
- Show the process listening on a TCP port:

`lsof -nP -iTCP:{{port}} -sTCP:LISTEN`

- Show files opened by a process:

`lsof -p {{pid}}`
@@tmux|common|Manage persistent terminal sessions.
- Create a named session:

`tmux new -s {{name}}`

- List sessions and attach to one:

`tmux ls && tmux attach -t {{name}}`
@@make|common|Run targets defined in a Makefile.
- Build the default target in parallel:

`make -j$(getconf _NPROCESSORS_ONLN 2>/dev/null || sysctl -n hw.ncpu)`

- Preview commands without running them:

`make --dry-run {{target}}`
@@ffmpeg|common|Convert and process audio and video.
- Convert a video to H.264 video and AAC audio:

`ffmpeg -i {{input}} -c:v libx264 -c:a aac {{output.mp4}}`

- Extract audio without re-encoding it:

`ffmpeg -i {{input.mp4}} -vn -c:a copy {{output.m4a}}`
@@sqlite3|common|Query SQLite databases.
- Open a database interactively:

`sqlite3 {{database.sqlite}}`

- Export a query as CSV with headers:

`sqlite3 -header -csv {{database.sqlite}} '{{SELECT * FROM table;}}'`
@@brew|osx|Install and manage software with Homebrew on macOS.
- Update metadata and upgrade installed formulae:

`brew update && brew upgrade`

- Find and install a package:

`brew search {{name}} && brew install {{formula}}`

- Diagnose common Homebrew problems:

`brew doctor`
@@open|osx|Open files, directories, and URLs with macOS applications.
- Open the current directory in Finder:

`open .`

- Open a file with a chosen application:

`open -a '{{Visual Studio Code}}' {{file}}`
@@pbcopy|osx|Copy standard input to the macOS clipboard.
- Copy a file's contents to the clipboard:

`pbcopy < {{file}}`

- Copy the current directory path:

`pwd | pbcopy`
@@defaults|osx|Read and write macOS application preferences.
- Read all preferences for an application domain:

`defaults read {{com.apple.finder}}`

- Write a string preference, then restart the application if needed:

`defaults write {{domain}} {{key}} -string '{{value}}'`
@@launchctl|osx|Inspect and control macOS launch services.
- List loaded jobs whose labels contain a word:

`launchctl list | grep -i '{{name}}'`

- Restart a user agent:

`launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/{{label}}`
@@diskutil|osx|Inspect and manage disks on macOS.
- List disks and volumes:

`diskutil list`

- Show detailed information about a volume:

`diskutil info {{/Volumes/Name}}`
@@apt|linux|Manage packages on Debian and Ubuntu.
- Refresh metadata and install available upgrades:

`sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade`

- Search for and install a package:

`apt search {{name}} && sudo apt install {{package}}`
@@dnf|linux|Manage packages on Fedora and related distributions.
- Upgrade installed packages:

`sudo dnf upgrade --refresh`

- Find which package provides a file or command:

`dnf provides '*/{{filename}}'`
@@pacman|linux|Manage packages on Arch Linux.
- Synchronize repositories and upgrade the system:

`sudo pacman -Syu`

- Search repositories and install a package:

`pacman -Ss {{name}} && sudo pacman -S {{package}}`
@@systemctl|linux|Control systemd services and units.
- Show status and recent messages for a service:

`systemctl status {{service}}`

- Enable a service at boot and start it now:

`sudo systemctl enable --now {{service}}`
@@journalctl|linux|Read logs collected by systemd-journald.
- Follow messages for a service:

`journalctl -fu {{service}}`

- Show high-priority messages since the current boot:

`journalctl -b -p err`
@@ip|linux|Inspect and configure Linux networking.
- Show addresses on all interfaces:

`ip address show`

- Show the routing table:

`ip route show`
@@ss|linux|Inspect Linux network sockets.
- Show listening TCP and UDP sockets with process details:

`sudo ss -tulpn`

- Show established TCP connections:

`ss -tn state established`
@@powershell|windows|Run PowerShell commands and scripts.
- Run a script while passing named arguments:

`powershell -File {{script.ps1}} -{{Name}} {{Value}}`

- Run one command and exit:

`powershell -NoProfile -Command "{{Get-Process}}"`
@@winget|windows|Install and manage Windows applications.
- Search for an application:

`winget search {{name}}`

- Install an exact package ID and accept prompts:

`winget install --exact --id {{Publisher.Package}} --accept-source-agreements --accept-package-agreements`
@@choco|windows|Manage Windows packages with Chocolatey.
- Search for and install a package:

`choco search {{name}} && choco install {{package}}`

- Upgrade all installed packages after reviewing the list:

`choco outdated && choco upgrade all`
@@robocopy|windows|Reliably copy directory trees on Windows.
- Mirror a source directory to a destination after a dry run:

`robocopy {{source}} {{destination}} /MIR /L`

- Copy recursively with restartable mode and a log:

`robocopy {{source}} {{destination}} /E /Z /LOG:{{copy.log}}`
@@tasklist|windows|List processes on Windows.
- List all processes:

`tasklist`

- Filter processes by executable name:

`tasklist /FI "IMAGENAME eq {{program.exe}}"`
@@taskkill|windows|Terminate Windows processes.
- End a process by its ID:

`taskkill /PID {{pid}}`

- Forcefully end a program and its child processes by name:

`taskkill /F /T /IM {{program.exe}}`
@@ipconfig|windows|Display and manage Windows network configuration.
- Display detailed configuration for every adapter:

`ipconfig /all`

- Clear the DNS resolver cache:

`ipconfig /flushdns`
@@wsl|windows|Run and manage Windows Subsystem for Linux distributions.
- List installed distributions and their versions:

`wsl --list --verbose`

- Run a command in a chosen distribution:

`wsl --distribution {{Ubuntu}} -- {{command}}`
@@ls|common|List directory contents.
- Show hidden entries with human-readable sizes:

`ls -lah {{directory}}`

- Sort entries by modification time, newest first:

`ls -lt {{directory}}`
@@cd|common|Change the current shell directory.
- Move to the parent directory:

`cd ..`

- Return to the previous directory:

`cd -`
@@pwd|common|Print the current directory path.
- Print the logical path, preserving symbolic links:

`pwd -L`

- Print the physical path after resolving symbolic links:

`pwd -P`
@@cp|common|Copy files and directories.
- Copy a file while preserving its metadata:

`cp -p {{source}} {{destination}}`

- Recursively copy a directory and show each file:

`cp -Rv {{source-directory}} {{destination-directory}}`
@@mv|common|Move or rename files and directories.
- Rename a file:

`mv {{old-name}} {{new-name}}`

- Ask before overwriting an existing destination:

`mv -i {{source}} {{destination}}`
@@rm|common|Remove files and directories.
- Ask before removing each selected file:

`rm -i {{file1 file2}}`

- Preview directory contents before considering recursive removal:

`find {{directory}} -maxdepth 2 -print`
@@mkdir|common|Create directories.
- Create a directory and any missing parents:

`mkdir -p {{path/to/directory}}`

- Create several sibling directories:

`mkdir {{one two three}}`
@@df|common|Show free and used filesystem space.
- Show human-readable space for all mounted filesystems:

`df -h`

- Show space for the filesystem containing a path:

`df -h {{path}}`
@@du|common|Estimate file and directory sizes.
- Show the total human-readable size of a directory:

`du -sh {{directory}}`

- Show the size of each immediate child, sorted numerically:

`du -sk {{directory}}/* | sort -n`
@@head|common|Print the beginning of files or input.
- Print the first 20 lines:

`head -n 20 {{file}}`

- Print the first 100 bytes:

`head -c 100 {{file}}`
@@tail|common|Print the end of files or follow appended data.
- Print the last 20 lines:

`tail -n 20 {{file}}`

- Follow a log, retrying if it is recreated:

`tail -F {{logfile}}`
@@less|common|Interactively view text one screen at a time.
- Open a file and show line numbers:

`less -N {{file}}`

- Follow growing input; press Ctrl-C to stop following:

`less +F {{logfile}}`
@@sort|common|Sort lines of text.
- Sort numbers from largest to smallest:

`sort -nr {{file}}`

- Sort a CSV-like file by its second field:

`sort -t, -k2,2 {{file}}`
@@uniq|common|Report or remove adjacent duplicate lines.
- Sort input, then count each unique line:

`sort {{file}} | uniq -c`

- Print only repeated adjacent lines:

`uniq -d {{sorted-file}}`
@@xargs|common|Build command invocations from standard input.
- Run one command per null-delimited filename:

`find {{directory}} -type f -print0 | xargs -0 -n1 {{command}}`

- Preview the commands that would be run:

`printf '%s\n' {{items}} | xargs -n1 echo {{command}}`
@@tee|common|Copy standard input to files and standard output.
- Save output while still displaying it:

`{{command}} | tee {{output.log}}`

- Append output to a file:

`{{command}} | tee -a {{output.log}}`
@@zip|common|Create and update ZIP archives.
- Recursively archive a directory:

`zip -r {{archive.zip}} {{directory}}`

- Add several files to an archive:

`zip {{archive.zip}} {{file1 file2}}`
@@unzip|common|List or extract ZIP archives.
- List archive contents without extracting:

`unzip -l {{archive.zip}}`

- Extract into a selected directory:

`unzip {{archive.zip}} -d {{destination}}`
